# platform.linux.storage.store

What the virtual chips keep their bytes in: a BlockStore interface, a
MemoryStore for tests, and a FileStore over std::filebuf. A FileStore opens an
existing file at its own size, or makes a missing one at the requested size
filled with a byte -- zeros for a new SD card, 0xFF for an erased flash chip
-- and flushes every write, so a program that is killed leaves the image as
consistent as the file system on it made it. Standard library only, so it
builds on the host lane.
